# Ignore everything at the repo root by default, then explicitly allow
# back in only this project's actual source tree. This is deliberately
# an allowlist, not a per-project-name list: `ai-film init`/`/create-film`
# creates a new top-level directory named after whatever film title you
# give it (e.g. `one-more-life/`, `hot-&-fierce-villain/`), and every one
# of those is a full film project — shot data, reference images, and
# possibly paid-for generated media — that must never be committed, no
# matter what a user names their film. Adding a new top-level source
# file/directory to this repo requires adding a matching `!/...` line
# below, or it silently won't be tracked.
/*

!/.claude/
!/docs/
!/src/
!/tests/
!/.gitignore
!/LICENSE
!/pyproject.toml
!/README.md
!/README.zh-TW.md

# Tooling/build artifacts that can appear nested inside the allowed
# directories above (e.g. src/ai_film/__pycache__/) and must stay
# ignored even though their parent directory is tracked.
.superpowers/
.claude/worktrees/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
build/
dist/
.env
.DS_Store
